OGRE 1.12.10: an OpenGL ES 2/3 render system on QNX Screen (EGL).

QNX has no desktop OpenGL and no GLX: graphics is OpenGL ES 2/3 through EGL
on Screen. OGRE's GLES2 render system runs on EGL, but its GLSupport layer
knows EGL only on Android, Emscripten, Windows and X11. This adds a QNX one
(RenderSystems/GLSupport/{include,src}/EGL/QNX): the default EGL display,
and render windows on a Screen window -- one OGRE creates, or one handed
over as "externalWindowHandle" (Qt's QWindow::winId() on its qnx platform
is the screen_window_t). On QNX the window's buffers are the application's
to create (screen_create_window_buffers) in the format of the EGL config's
native visual before eglCreateWindowSurface, and to recreate at every size
change; Screen allocates 8-bit RGBX/RGBA buffers only, while Mesa lists its
10-bit configs first (docs/porting-hazards.md #157), so the window picks an
8-bit config in one of those visuals itself. A swap that fails (the window
was resized under the surface) makes the buffers and surface again; a
hidden window (setHidden) is not visible, so OGRE does not draw and swap it.

Also:
- EGLSupport::createNewContext: share every context with the main one, as
  OGRE's other GL platforms do. It created the second and later windows'
  contexts unshared, so a window made after the first (RViz's views, after
  its hidden 1x1 window) saw none of the textures, buffers and programs.
- glesw/GLES2RenderSystem: take the core GL ES functions from libGLESv2.so.1
  with dlsym (as on Android); eglGetProcAddress is only required to return
  extension functions, and QNX images have no unversioned libGLESv2.so.
- EGLContext::_updateInternalResources (Android only): also on QNX, to point
  a context at a recreated surface.
- CMake: plugins without the "lib" prefix (OGRE's loader asks for
  RenderSystem_GLES2.so; CMake calls q++ "QCC", not GNU); no X11 and no
  libpthread on QNX (threads are in libc).

Upstream-Status: Pending
